            "block_content": "SECTION 9.13. Termination allowance normally will be paid according to the Company's payroll procedures for the hours equivalent to the employee's regular work week to the extent of the total allowance granted. LUMP SUM PAYMENT WILL BE MADE ONLY WHEREIN IT BECOMES CONDITIONAL UPON SUCH PAYMENT THAT NO FURTHER OBLIGATION RESTS UPON THE COMPANY WITH RESPECT TO THAT FORMER EMPLOYEE. Employees are entitled to no other benefits when on lay-off except those covered under Article 8, Section 8.4, and under this Article 9.",
